<figure class="wp-block-image alignwide size-large"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1024" height="512" src="https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/Picture121-1024x512.jpg" alt="An abandoned, decaying factory complex." class="wp-image-1275" srcset="https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/Picture121-1024x512.jpg 1024w, https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/Picture121-300x150.jpg 300w, https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/Picture121-768x384.jpg 768w, https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/Picture121-1536x768.jpg 1536w, https://www.americanyawp.com/textbook/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/Picture121.jpg 1600w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption class="wp-element-caption">Abandoned Packard Automotive Plant in Detroit, Michigan. Via <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Abandoned_Packard_Automobile_Factory_Detroit_200.jpg">Wikimedia</a>.</figcaption></figure>







